---
title: "Infinite backrooms"
note: "A found-footage horror film that writes itself. The camera walks the Backrooms, nearly sixty levels of them, three at a time, and on the way things happen: a phone rings and stops, footsteps fall into step behind, the date stamp jumps, a mirror shows the room without the camera. After every third level there is a 40% chance that something finds it: one of forty things of orrery's own (faceless office workers, listening dogs with human hands, a mascot that runs too fast, a deer of light) or now and then an SCP. How it shows itself is rolled, and what it is decides how the camera gets away: it looks away, holds its breath, runs (and is sometimes caught: the tape tears, rewinds, and the walk starts again in the yellow rooms), flees through the water, hides, holds it off with the camera light, follows where it leads, or is simply shown a kindness. Every way out noclips into a new level, forty ways of it, and the walk goes on. CUT TO: lines steer it; another seed is another film. The SCPs come from the SCP Wiki (CC BY-SA 3.0, credited in __scp/entities__)."
tags: [loops, h3, reel, goto, horror, motion_context]
---
@h3 text 16:9
context: 22
style: found footage from a 1990s VHS camcorder, one continuous unbroken ten-second shot: soft smeared colour, faint tracking lines, the date stamp "JUN 14 1996 3:12 AM" in the lower corner, handheld at chest height
MUSIC: N/A

SCENE the yellow rooms
$level = __backrooms/levels#start:yes__
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
SHOT 10s: push in, slow
The camera operator walks slowly forward through $level. The place is completely empty and goes on in every direction.
SFX: $level.sfx; the camera operator's breathing and footsteps close to the microphone
END ON: $exit

SCENE the walk ×3
$level = __backrooms/levels__
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
$event = {__backrooms/events__:3|none:2}
$contact = {40% contact}
SHOT 10s: {push in, slow|tracking, slow|push in, small, slow|pan left, slow|pan right, slow}
$exit[-1].open, into $level, which goes on in every direction. The camera operator walks slowly on{IF $event is not none: ; $event|}.
SFX: $level.sfx{IF $event is not none: ; $event.sfx|}; the camera operator's breathing and footsteps close to the microphone
END ON: $exit
IF $contact is contact: CUT TO: contact
CUT TO: the walk

# What finds the camera, and how it shows itself; what it is decides the way out.
SCENE contact
$thing = {__backrooms/entities__:4|__scp/entities__}
$level = __backrooms/levels__
SHOT 10s: static
$exit[-1].open, into $level. The camera operator stops dead: $thing __backrooms/approaches__. The camera trembles in the operator's hands.
SFX: $thing.sfx; the operator's breath catching; the fluorescent buzz rising
END ON: the thing stands between the camera and the way on
IF $thing.escape is look-away: CUT TO: eyes shut
IF $thing.escape is silence: CUT TO: silence
IF $thing.escape is chase: CUT TO: the chase
IF $thing.escape is water: CUT TO: the deep floor
IF $thing.escape is hide: CUT TO: hiding
IF $thing.escape is light: CUT TO: the light
IF $thing.escape is follow: CUT TO: following
CUT TO: a kindness

SCENE eyes shut
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
SHOT 10s: tilt down, fast
The camera swings down to the floor before it can look straight at $thing[-1]. The operator squeezes their eyes shut; the picture shows only the floor and shaking hands while the thing $thing[-1].meet. Then the operator stumbles forward, and $exit.
SFX: $thing[-1].sfx very close; the operator's ragged, held breath
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE silence
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
$hide = __backrooms/hides__
SHOT 10s: static, small
The operator crouches behind $hide and holds their breath. $thing[-1] $thing[-1].meet. The operator slips out the other way, and $exit.
SFX: total silence but for $thing[-1].sfx; one drop of water falling
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE the chase
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
$fate = {70% gone|caught}
SHOT 10s: tracking, fast
The operator turns and runs, the camera jolting wildly, __backrooms/routes__, while $thing[-1] $thing[-1].meet.
IF $fate is gone: At the last moment $exit, and the noise behind stops.
IF $fate is caught: A huge shape fills the frame from the side, the camera is torn away and tumbles across the floor, still recording.
SFX: running footsteps; $thing[-1].sfx right behind; the camera's case cracking
END ON: the picture jolts and breaks up for a moment
IF $fate is caught: CUT TO: the tape
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE the deep floor
$exit = __backrooms/exits[open=The camera rises dripping out of shallow water]__
SHOT 10s: push in, slow
The floor ahead is flooded with dark water. $thing[-1] $thing[-1].meet; the operator holds the camera high and backs away until $exit, the picture going green and murky.
SFX: water rushing into the microphone; $thing[-1].sfx muffled through the water
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE hiding
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
$hide = __backrooms/hides__
SHOT 10s: static, small
The operator backs into $hide and pulls the camera in close. Through a gap the picture shows $thing[-1], which $thing[-1].meet. When it is gone, the operator creeps out, and $exit.
SFX: $thing[-1].sfx coming closer, then going away; the operator's heartbeat close to the microphone
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE the light
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
SHOT 10s: push in, small
The operator flicks on the camera's light and holds the beam straight on $thing[-1], which $thing[-1].meet. Keeping the beam on it, the operator backs away, and $exit.
SFX: the camera light clicking on; $thing[-1].sfx
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE following
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
SHOT 10s: tracking, slow
$thing[-1] $thing[-1].meet. The operator follows at a distance, room after room, until it stops beside a door and is gone, and $exit.
SFX: $thing[-1].sfx ahead; the operator's careful footsteps
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE a kindness
$exit = __backrooms/exits__
SHOT 10s: static
$thing[-1] $thing[-1].meet. The operator, still shaking, laughs in spite of everything, walks on, and $exit.
SFX: $thing[-1].sfx; the operator's shaky laughter
END ON: $exit
CUT TO: the walk

SCENE the tape
SHOT 10s: static
The picture is all tracking noise and static. The tape counter spins backwards, the date stamp flickers, and the static slowly clears into the yellow rooms again, as if the tape had been rewound.
SFX: tape hiss; the whir of a cassette rewinding; a click
END ON: the camera stands again at the start of the yellow rooms
CUT TO: the yellow rooms
